# THE USER'S 24-HOUR SETTING REACHING THE DOOR (docs/compliance-plan.md §4):
# the format guest with the platform's own clock knob flipped BY THE LANE —
# Apple's AppleICUForce24HourTime in this process's argument domain, written
# by the core from KAYA_CLOCK since a launch argument does not reach a guest
# that formats before its defaults exist; `settings put system time_12_24 24`
# on Android; the Region keys iTime and sShortTime on Windows; GNOME's
# clock-format through a keyfile settings backend in the container. The
# cycle is read back from the platform's own setting, which a knob that
# failed to reach it cannot satisfy, and the label is the platform's own
# rendering under it — Windows writes left-to-right marks between the
# fields, so no stored string could hold on five lanes.
expect_hour_cycle 24
expect label#3 "{fmt:time 08:30 short}"
